{
  "scene_id": "video03_scene05_error_minimization",
  "video_title": "Supervised Learning",
  "scene_title": "Error Minimization",
  "order": 5,
  "duration_mode": "audio_driven",
  "voice": {
    "language": "en-IN",
    "speaker": "priya",
    "model": "bulbul:v3"
  },
  "narration": [
    {
      "id": "s5_01",
      "text": "The model doesn't just want any line… it wants the best line."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5_02",
      "text": "You'll see a vertical gap between that point and our line. This distance is the Error."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5_03",
      "text": "Mathematically, it's just the actual value minus the predicted value."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5_04",
      "text": "We need to look at all the points. These residuals appear for every single student."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5_05",
      "text": "Some errors are positive, some negative. If we added them up, they'd cancel out."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5_06",
      "text": "So we square them. Imagine each error bar expanding into a square."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5_07",
      "text": "Larger mistakes count much, much more. A small miss is fine, but a huge miss is penalized heavily."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5_08",
      "text": "Mean Squared Error. We take all those squared errors, add them up, and find the average. Loss. Cost."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5_09",
      "text": "Watch that Cost indicator in the corner. As the model tweaks the weight and bias…"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5_10",
      "text": "The line shifts into a better position… that cost number starts to shrink."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5_11",
      "text": "Once the cost stops shrinking and the line becomes stable, we've found our best fit."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5_12",
      "text": "But sometimes, being too accurate on our current data can actually be a problem."
    }
  ],
